{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"agent_message","text":"A persistent fused kernel now computes the routing gradient and `grad_hidden_states` together, reusing each token’s 128-way gradient across all 2,048 output columns. It is about 25–30% faster than the separate prefix-plus-GEMM path for the common token counts and matches the reference cast/reduction behavior; I’m integrating it for sizes where it wins and retaining the library path for larger matrices."}}
