{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"agent_message","text":"The third verification confirms the cheaper sparse formulation is the main win at large sizes (65k tokens improved from 307 µs to 251 µs). The persistent small-size fusion did not beat the library path under the verifier’s timing method, so I’m testing one final, more aggressive option locally: compute both outputs in a single mixed-work kernel, eliminating the remaining inter-kernel dependency and launch. I’ll only keep it if it clearly wins and preserves the matched ratio."}}
